name: surface-teaches-outweigh-model-invention
kind: inferred
shape: categorical
face: in
membrane: false
note: when a model invents wire syntax that does not exist ({{ r.flights[*] }}
  wildcards, literal re-typing of bound values), the fix that lands is
  explicit surface text — grammar rules, guide rows, seed programs — not
  capability work, because the surface already supports the honest spelling.
  Two measured instances 2026-11-23: splice wildcards banned in VALUES,
  say-shape doctrine moved always-on after guides proved structurally unable
  to reach terminal composition. The signal marks that a model's invention
  is evidence about teaching coverage, not about missing machinery.
